@startuml
title Data Flow Diagram - Sensor Reading to Alert and Dashboard

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontColor #1F2937
skinparam componentBorderColor #374151
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam databaseBorderColor #059669
skinparam databaseBackgroundColor #ECFDF5
skinparam actorBorderColor #374151
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam noteBorderColor #D97706
skinparam arrowColor #374151

left to right direction

note as Purpose
  Purpose:
  Shows how data moves through the system: sensor readings become
  tagged telemetry, telemetry becomes processed features, features
  become health decisions, and abnormal decisions become alerts.
end note

actor "Machine" as Machine
component "P1 Capture Sensor Data\nESP32 reads temp + vibration" as P1
component "P2 Tag + Validate\nmachineId, sensorId, timestamp" as P2
component "P3 Publish Telemetry\nMQTT over Wi-Fi" as P3
component "P4 Ingest + Store\nGateway/cloud receiver" as P4
component "P5 Process + Extract Features\nclean, RMS, average, peaks" as P5
component "P6 Analyze Health\nrules / ML model" as P6
component "P7 Generate Alert\nseverity + recommendation" as P7
component "P8 Display Dashboard\ntrends, KPIs, alerts" as P8
actor "Maintenance\nOperator" as Operator

database "D1 Raw Telemetry" as D1
database "D2 Processed Features" as D2
database "D3 Predictions + Alerts" as D3
database "D4 Maintenance History" as D4

Machine --> P1 : heat + vibration signals
P1 --> P2 : raw sensor values
P2 --> P3 : valid tagged record
P3 --> P4 : MQTT topic\nfactory/{machineId}/telemetry
P4 --> D1 : save raw records
P4 --> P5 : telemetry stream
P5 --> D2 : save feature windows
P5 --> P6 : feature vector
P6 --> D3 : health state + risk score
P6 --> P7 : degrading / faulty / critical state
P7 --> D3 : alert event
P7 --> P3 : MQTT alert topic\nfactory/{machineId}/alert
P8 --> D1 : query readings
P8 --> D2 : query trends
P8 --> D3 : query alerts
P8 --> D4 : query maintenance status
P8 --> Operator : machine status + action cue
Operator --> P8 : acknowledge alert\nupdate maintenance action
Operator --> D4 : inspection / repair note

legend bottom
|= DFD Element |= Meaning |
| P1..P8 | Processing step in the telemetry-to-alert pipeline |
| D1..D4 | Data store used by dashboard, analytics, or maintenance review |
| MQTT telemetry topic | Upstream machine readings from ESP32 to gateway/cloud |
| MQTT alert topic | Downstream alert or command from cloud/gateway to ESP32 |
| Operator flow | Human acknowledgement and maintenance feedback loop |
endlegend
@enduml
